msgid "Tests and Transactions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use the standard Quarkus `@Transactional` annotation on tests, but "
"this means that the changes your\n"
"test makes to the database will be persistent. If you want any changes made "
"to be rolled back at the end of\n"
"the test you can use the `io.quarkus.test.TestTransaction` annotation. This "
"will run the test method in a\n"
"transaction, but roll it back once the test method is complete to revert any "
"database changes."
msgstr ""

